Hello, and welcome to TechScape. I=E2=80=99m your host, Blake Montgomery, w=
riting to you as I sit under yellowing leaves in New York. Today in tech, w=
e=E2=80=99re discussing technocracy.

Trump entwines his power with AI

Donald Trump made a series of moves over the past week that make it clear h=
is power is becoming synonymous with artificial intelligence.

The new tight alliances between the White House, the Pentagon, US intellige=
nce agencies and AI companies loom ominously over governments and companies=
, particularly in Europe, that rely on American AI.

Last Tuesday, Trump and six AI CEOs signed what he called a =E2=80=9Cmorall=
y binding=E2=80=9D agreement to put controls on artificial intelligence. Th=
e vague agreement stipulates a framework for what Trump called =E2=80=9Ctre=
mendous self-policing=E2=80=9D, reiterating his point that AI companies can=
 act as their own watchmen. Elon Musk, Mark Zuckerberg, Jensen Huang and Da=
rio Amodei signed.

Zuckerberg hand-guided the writing of that agreement,
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR9VQ=
fZMZ-RwR2nuxBv6aaHHFFjHnnXJaPSgFd4fn83SUSwoP5CsJ7BRGRWN1I0yHZ6LkI0fqHIuLanc=
WV4fgs5uHCS-mBf_FQ1d8woJ4i-nwxmd2BshiTVbgnZ3DVLyX0I_2ru0c9rqctLRsEckgPrGasa=
