<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Employees across the globe are increasingl=
y finding themselves minutely monitored in their workplaces, with tiny chan=
ges in their behaviors resulting in negative performance evaluations.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The latest example of workers under survei=
llance and bristling at it comes from Co-op, which operates supermarkets, u=
ndertakers, insurance and legal services companies in the UK. The company i=
mplemented an automated listening technology that rates every phone call so=
me of them make to customers.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In a system described as =E2=80=9Coppressi=
ve and dystopian=E2=80=9D by a whistleblower, Co-op Legal Services is using=
 AI models to record, analyze and award a percentage score for interactions=
 between agents and customers seeking advice about probate, wills and estat=
es.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CYou are being watched,=E2=80=9D s=
aid a Co-op worker who spoke to the Guardian on condition of anonymity.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Read more: <a href=3D"https://abli=
nk.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszc=
